abstract: >-
  PyVWF is an open-source Python framework that simulates
  bias-corrected wind power generation from reanalysis data (e.g. ERA5). It
  re-implements the Virtual Wind Farm (VWF) methodology used by
  Renewables.ninja, exposing the full training and application workflow for
  bias-correction factors at turbine, regional, or national scale, with
  configurable spatial clustering and temporal aggregation.
keywords:
  - wind energy
  - virtual wind farm
  - bias correction
  - capacity factor
  - renewable energy
  - reanalysis
